# held/weapons/axe: the bearded axe (art weapon 2, `held axe.bearded`): an ash haft of 13 px (2 px of wood, the lit line step 3, the shade step 2), a leather wrap under the fist and a 5 x 6 bearded head, its steel edge line facing the swing and its cheek dark (P2c wave 2, WEAPONS). STYLE_P2 11 / 25.7; P2C_CONTRACTS 4: the library weapon on the grip,
# a000..a337 = degrees counter-clockwise from screen-right, drawn once (D) for every facing; facing L its own views (the head mirrored, so the edge faces the swing); origin = the grip point
# under the main fist (the hand is drawn over the grip); `mark tip` at the far end. Drafted with the area's stepper (exact
# 1:0, 2:1, 1:1 and 1:2 runs, the top-left light by rule: a 2 px band's upper / left line lit) and hand-cleaned at 12x.
# Finish regions (contracts 3b): R the head's socket, N the wrap.
use person
body adult
role held axe.bearded
layer held
anchor grip
keys held
tags anyfacing
